1. MINIMAL WITNESS: exhaustive search for >=2 circuit sign changes
==========================================================================
  smallest degree with >=2 sign changes in this pool: d = 5
  N(n) = (n+1)^2 (n+3)^2 (n+8)^1
    R_1 =          256/215 = 1.190697674419
    R_2 =        1849/1600 = 1.155625000000
    R_3 =       10000/8643 = 1.157005669328
    R_4 =        4489/4000 = 1.122250000000
  sign(c_2..c_4) = -+-   sign changes = 2
  curvature C(mu)  = +0.14135742
  curvature C(mu*) = +0.41294497
  Both end curvatures positive => the classifier PREDICTS 'interior maximum',
  i.e. exactly one sign change.  The truth is two.  CLASSIFIER REFUTED.
  All roots are real and positive: PF-infinity, Hurwitz, strictly ULC.
  VERDICT 1: REFUTED (witness verified, Newton R_k>1 throughout)

==========================================================================
2. CLUSTER LAW: max sign changes with m well-separated clusters = 2m-3
==========================================================================
    m   best sizes found      max sign changes    predicted 2m-3
    1   None                         0                 0         OK
    2   [3, 2]                       1                 1         OK
    3   [4, 5, 2]                    3                 3         OK
    4   [5, 4, 5, 3]                 5                 5         OK
    5   [5, 2, 3, 4, 4]              7                 7         OK
    6   [2, 3, 4, 4, 3, 4]           9                 9         OK
  mechanism: c_k ~ -Delta^2(sorted log-root step function); a step function
  with m-1 kinks has 2(m-1) alternating second-difference spikes, and the
  boundary trims exactly one, leaving 2m-3.
  VERDICT 2: CLUSTER LAW CONFIRMED AND ATTAINED

